    "created_at": "2016-11-10T16:46:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-10T16:46:48Z",
    "body": "> OK, what about subclassing multicol?\n\nTo be clear, this is the same as subclassing `asdf`, right?\n\nThe idea of subclassing is to subclass elements defined in HTML as having useful UA behavior. `asdf` or, to my knowledge, `multicol`, are not such elements.\n\nThere's a small forward-compatibility argument here too, as if we allowed subclassing `asdf`, and authors did so on the assumption they were not going to inherit any interesting behavior, and then in the future we made `asdf` do something interesting, that could break author assumptions.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/259742114/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
      "-1": 0,
