    "created_at": "2016-11-10T17:04:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-10T17:04:04Z",
    "body": "> To be clear, this is the same as subclassing asdf, right?\n\nNot quite, since multicol has interesting things in UA stylesheets...  and I guess bgsound could in theory still be supported by some UA.\n\n> There's a small forward-compatibility argument here too\n\nThat's a much stronger argument, from my point of view.  So the point is we explicitly do not want to support subclassing of elements that have no current semantics, for future compat reasons.  That makes sense; would be good to have that documented clearly.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
